@UserManagementAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5028

### 1. Obtener usuarios paginados por defecto (200 OK)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Obtener usuarios con paginación explícita (200 OK)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users?page=1&pageSize=2
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Filtrar usuarios por departamento TI y activos (200 OK)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users?department=TI&isActive=true&page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Paginación inválida (400 Bad Request)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users?page=0&pageSize=500
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Obtener un usuario por ID existente (200 OK)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Obtener usuario con ID no positivo (400 Bad Request)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/0
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Obtener usuario con ID negativo (400 Bad Request)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/-5
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Obtener un usuario inexistente (404 Not Found)
GET {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Crear un nuevo usuario válido (201 Created)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Lucía",
  "lastName": "Fernández",
  "email": "lucia.fernandez@techhive.com",
  "department": "RR.HH.",
  "role": "Coordinadora de Nómina",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 10. Crear usuario con nombre relleno de espacios demasiado corto (400 Bad Request)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "  A  ",
  "lastName": "Sánchez",
  "email": "a.sanchez@techhive.com",
  "department": "TI",
  "role": "Analista",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 11. Crear usuario con correo sin TLD válido (400 Bad Request)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Pedro",
  "lastName": "Sánchez",
  "email": "usuario@dominio",
  "department": "TI",
  "role": "Analista",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 12. Crear usuario con correo duplicado (409 Conflict)
POST {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ana",
  "lastName": "Duplicada",
  "email": "ana.gomez@techhive.com",
  "department": "RR.HH.",
  "role": "Reclutadora",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 13. Actualizar un usuario existente (200 OK)
PUT {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/4
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Lucía",
  "lastName": "Fernández Vargas",
  "email": "lucia.fernandez@techhive.com",
  "department": "RR.HH.",
  "role": "Gerente de Nómina",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 14. Actualizar con ID no positivo (400 Bad Request)
PUT {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/0
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Lucía",
  "lastName": "Fernández",
  "email": "lucia.fernandez@techhive.com",
  "department": "RR.HH.",
  "role": "Gerente de Nómina",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 15. Actualizar un usuario inexistente (404 Not Found)
PUT {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "No",
  "lastName": "Existe",
  "email": "no.existe@techhive.com",
  "department": "TI",
  "role": "Empleado",
  "isActive": false
}

###

### 16. Eliminar usuario con ID negativo (400 Bad Request)
DELETE {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/-1
Accept: application/json

###

### 17. Eliminar usuario creado (204 No Content)
DELETE {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/4
Accept: application/json

###

### 18. Eliminar usuario inexistente (404 Not Found)
DELETE {{UserManagementAPI_HostAddress}}/api/users/999
Accept: application/json
